{title: John Henry}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
When [G]John Henry was a little baby,
[C]Sitting on his daddy's [G]knee,
He picked up a hammer and a little piece of steel,
Said [D7]hammer's going to be the death of [G]me, Lord, Lord,
[D7]Hammer's going to be the death of [G]me.

{c: Verse 2}
The [G]captain said to John Henry,
Gonna [C]bring that steam drill [G]round,
Gonna bring that steam drill out on the job,
Gonna [D7]whop that steel on [G]down, Lord, Lord,
Gonna [D7]whop that steel on [G]down.

{c: Verse 3}
[G]John Henry told his captain,
A [C]man ain't nothing but a [G]man,
But before I let your steam drill beat me down,
I'll [D7]die with my hammer in my [G]hand, Lord, Lord,
I'll [D7]die with my hammer in my [G]hand.
